            0.521,
            0.072,
            0.813,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Propositions and their Converses"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.864,
            0.071,
            0.88,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.111,
            0.852,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To clearly understand this, let us reframe the argument as follows —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.134,
            0.146,
            0.152
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.134,
            0.662,
            0.152
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n has an odd number of factors"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.153,
            0.583,
            0.19
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathbf { w h i c h \\; i m p l i e s }\\tag{ii}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.172,
            0.737,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the existence of a factor-partner pair in which the"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.192,
            0.665,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "same number repeats, say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( f , f )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.229,
            0.647,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) n is a square number: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n = f \\times f"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.254,
            0.88,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This only proves Q. It doesn’t prove that every square number has an odd number of factors (Proposition P)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.293,
            0.262,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is P true?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.311,
            0.754,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is. The argument above can be modified to prove this."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.33,
            0.882,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We start with (iii). Clearly, (iii) implies (ii). Does (ii) imply (i)? Not necessarily because (ii) does not state the number of pairs with repeating factors. For example, if the number of such pairs is two — say "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline { { \\mathcal { f } } } , \\mathcal { f }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and (g, g) — what can we say about the number of factors? In such a case, the given number will have an even number of factors."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.427,
            0.881,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "However, a number cannot have more than one factor pair with repeating factors. Thus, a square number necessarily has an odd number of factors. Hence Statement P is also true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.483,
            0.882,
            0.522
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this example, ‘n is a perfect square’ and ‘n has an odd number of factors’ imply each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.523,
            0.286,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.54,
            0.881,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Proposition P: If two triangles have the same area, then they are congruent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.58,
            0.881,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Converse Q: If two triangles are congruent, then they have the same area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.623,
            0.881,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Determine if these statements are true or not. Justify the true statements and give a counterexample for each false statement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.667,
            0.881,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These examples show that a proposition can be true but not its converse. Or it can happen that both the proposition and its converse are true."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.739,
            0.399,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.776,
            0.851,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It can also happen that both the proposition and converse are false! Can you give an example?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
